From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:01:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(llama-cpp): Free parks a model that can park, and a full
 device answers RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED

Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside the others
(patches/0023-server-park-when-told.patch), with the backend's side here.

A model that takes context on demand, on a device whose weight buffers can
leave it and come back (SYCL with GGML_SYCL_PARKABLE=1), no longer has to
be stopped to give its device memory back. With LocalAI's own two calls,
and no new one:

- Free PARKS it: the context is freed, the weights are copied to host
  memory and leave the device; the process, its tokenizer and everything
  validated at the load stay. The answer is success with the message
  "parked" and, in metadata, {"parked":true,"park_size":<bytes>,"ms":..}.
- LoadModel for the model the process already holds brings the weights
  back, then answers what it always answered, byte for byte: "Model
  already loaded". Not parked, it is the no-op it was.
- a request to a parked model brings the weights back by itself, and they
  then stay on the device: a request never parks.
- Status says where the weights are. memory.total stays what a caller
  reads for a backend with no Status - the process's virtual size, as
  LocalAI's own sample, with "rss" - and the breakdown adds "parked",
  "park_size", "parked_host", "parks", "unparks" and "no_room".

"Model already loaded" is said only to the options that ARE loaded. This
backend compared the model's NAME alone, so a LoadModel under the same
name and other options was answered success while the old options went on
computing - harmless while nothing sent a second LoadModel, not once that
call is how a parked model comes back. The options of the load are kept;
a repeat that differs is refused FAILED_PRECONDITION, nothing is brought
back or loaded, and the message names the FIELDS that differ, never their
values: load options can carry credentials.

A model that cannot park answers Free and Status with Unimplemented, as
this backend always did: the caller stops the process, and samples it, as
before. Free while a request runs, or while the first load runs, answers
FailedPrecondition "busy" - it is for now, where Unimplemented is for good
- and the model stays as it is. A park that cannot copy the weights out
answers Internal, and they stay on the device.

One status for "the device has no room now". When parked weights cannot
come back, when a context cannot be created, or when the backend cannot
allocate memory for a graph, the request - Predict, PredictStream,
Embedding, Rerank, TTS, Score, the slot cache, a decision, a realtime
session - and a repeated LoadModel are answered RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED, where
they were INTERNAL like a fault. Nothing is wrong with the request or the
model; the same request can be sent again. Not UNAVAILABLE, which LocalAI
reads as a backend it can no longer reach. A return that FAILS - the
device failing, or bytes read back that are not the ones parked - is
INTERNAL: it is never answered as a refusal. Every other error is
INTERNAL, as before.

RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED has other meanings on this wire - a stream that is
busy, a message over the size limit, a rate-limited upstream - so the
refusal also says its type at the head of its message, where a caller
that maps statuses can tell it from them without a list of messages:
"no_room_on_device: the weights cannot come back to the device now".

A stream that fails after its first chunk ends with the error's status
(the commit before this one made it end as a failure at all): a refusal
of the moment in the middle of an answer is RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED there too.

The messages and the codes are in park_reply.h, tested without a model
(park_reply_test.cpp): a proxy in front of a backend tells a return from a
load by the bytes of "Model already loaded". prepare.sh probes the
checkout (LOCALAI_HAS_PARK), so a fork without the llama.cpp patch builds
this file as before, Free and Status unimplemented.

Checked without a device, on a CPU build of this backend with a stand-in
for a device that parks, refuses, fails and cannot park (a dev patch, in
no build): 49 of 49 over gRPC - a model that cannot park answers as
before; the same name under other options is refused with the fields
named and nothing of their contents, parked or not; Free, Status and
LoadModel as above; the first vectors bit for bit over 12 cycles; a
refused return is RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED "no_room_on_device: ..." with the
model still parked and the next request served; a FAILED return is
INTERNAL, still parked, counted as no refusal; weights that came back for
a request whose context is refused stay, one park and one copy in all; a
park that fails is INTERNAL with nothing parked; some 300 calls of Free
beside live requests, each done or refused busy, every request's vectors
intact; a stream refused a graph after its first chunk ends
RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED and the next one is whole. NOT run: any of it on a
device, or through LocalAI's server, which today calls Free only before
it stops a process.

